  ],
  "notes": "Cause code left TBD/provisional per FORM-366 fields (official code not provided). Two parallel failure paths from the 230kV Bus 1 isolation are modeled: (1) KD-10/KC-2 series trip circuit leading to generator/turbine/reactor trip, and (2) direct bus loss leading to failed fast bus transfer and RCP deenergization; both converge on the same Consequence node. AFW and 1B EDG are modeled as automatic actuations described as occurring during the event (not merely design-basis backups), so BACKED_UP_BY-style qualifying language was insufficiently explicit for a formal BACKED_UP_BY edge to the Consequence; they are captured via INVOLVES and referenced in the chain summary/reporting basis instead, consistent with rule 6's caution regarding ambiguous operability language. No previous similar event was cited (explicitly stated none in last three years), so no SIMILAR_TO edge or stub LER emitted."
